Annual budget planning and approval cycle

   1. Late July / Early August

Finalize the current-year budget and establish the preliminary budget for
the following fiscal year to support tuition planning.

   2. By October 1

Release tuition rates based on the preliminary planning assumptions.

   3. February / March

Review the upcoming year's preliminary budget using updated enrollment
expectations, with particular attention to teacher compensation and
staffing.

   4. By May 31

Obtain preliminary information from the church regarding significant
capital projects and shared-cost changes affecting future budget cycles.

*Example: Any shared capital projects given to the school by 5/31/2027 will
be included in the FY 28/29 budget and cannot commence or expect shared
contribution until 6/1/2028 so that we can plan for those costs.*

   5. Late July / Early August

Finalize the upcoming school year's budget using updated enrollment
information and establish the next preliminary planning budget.

--0000000000007830d206601c9701
